那名男子手里拿着一支烟，向西奥多西借火。随后他便继续前行。他不是他们预期的那个人。几个小时过去了，直到很明显交易不会发生。要么是凶手从未出现，要么是他们意识到这是一个圈套。在处理我们所谓的“嗜血狂魔”时，警方必须迅速采取行动，以防止更多的女性被谋杀和残害。各种疯狂的谣言四起，有人声称这些残害行为是盗墓的死灵法师所为。

26
00:17:35.000 --> 00:18:15.000
sorcerers who were digging up graves. Others feared that an unidentified serial killer known as Metal Fang had arrived in Kishinev to continue his spree. Some turned their suspicions towards theodosius Glukarev himself. Word was circulating that he had recently cut ties with a criminal group who were now using the extortions as a method of intimidation. With all these leads and more having reached dead ends, investigators revisited the evidence, beginning with the two extortion letters.
其他人则担心一个被称为“金属獠牙”的身份不明的连环杀手已经抵达基希讷乌继续作案。有些人将怀疑转向了西奥多西·格卢卡列夫本人。有传言称他最近切断了与一个犯罪团伙的联系，该团伙现在正利用勒索作为恐吓手段。随着所有这些线索及其他线索都陷入死胡同，调查人员重新审视了证据，从两封勒索信开始。

27
00:18:15.000 --> 00:19:06.000
Everything was niggling at one particular investigator. As he agonised over each word of the letters, the realisation suddenly dawned. In both notes the author had referred to Theodosius by his nickname, Fedos. Upon further questioning, Theodosius revealed that he didn't like his full name and would generally ask colleagues and associates to call him Fedor for short. In turn, close friends and family took to calling him Fedos. Realising the killer was amongst Theodosius' immediate circle, investigators narrowed down the list of suspects until just one person remained.
一切都让一位调查人员感到困惑。当他苦苦思索信中的每一个字时，他突然恍然大悟。在两张字条中，作者都称呼西奥多西为他的昵称“费多斯”（Fedos）。经过进一步询问，西奥多西透露他不喜欢自己的全名，通常会要求同事和熟人叫他“费多尔”（Fedor）作为简称。反过来，亲密的朋友和家人开始叫他“费多斯”。意识到凶手就在西奥多西的亲近圈子里，调查人员缩小了嫌疑人名单，直到只剩下一人。

28
00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:51.000
A few years earlier, Dmitri Kuzinsev was enjoying his wedding reception when he realised his new wife wasn't by his side. He searched the venue and eventually found her in a compromising position with another man. The man was Dmitri's second cousin, Theodosius Glukarev. Enraged, Dmitri chased Theodosius with a knife threatening to kill him. The guests disarmed Dmitri and tied him down before he could inflict any injuries. As Theodosius was led from the party, Dmitri shouted that he would find him and cut him.
几年前，德米特里·库津采夫（Dmitri Kuzinsev）正在享受他的婚宴时，发现新婚妻子不在身边。他搜寻了会场，最终发现她与另一个男人举止亲密。那个男人是德米特里的表弟，西奥多西·格卢卡列夫。德米特里大怒，拿着刀追赶西奥多西，威胁要杀了他。客人们在德米特里造成伤害前解除了他的武装并将他捆绑起来。当西奥多西被带离聚会时，德米特里大喊他会找到他并砍了他。

29
00:19:51.000 --> 00:20:32.000
Investigators explored Dmitri's background and discovered that he was already on the radar of the Soviet financial police, having been suspected of the theft and illegal sale of rare Soviet property. He also worked as a dining car manager for Soviet railways, which was significant given the killer had named the Kishinev train station as the extortion money drop site. Undercover officers boarded Dmitri's train in order to confront him, one disguised as a railway inspector spotted Dmitri and called him by name. Sensing he was in trouble, Dmitri jumped from the train and ran.
调查人员深入调查了德米特里的背景，发现他已经在苏联金融警察的监视之下，因涉嫌盗窃和非法销售稀有苏联财产而受到怀疑。他还担任苏联铁路的餐车经理，考虑到凶手将基希讷乌火车站定为勒索金投放点，这一点意义重大。便衣警察登上了德米特里的火车以便与他对质，一名伪装成铁路检查员的警察发现了德米特里并叫出了他的名字。感觉到有麻烦，德米特里跳下火车逃跑了。

30
00:20:32.000 --> 00:21:19.000
The chase was short-lived as Dmitri tripped over the tracks and was swiftly apprehended. Dmitri denied any wrongdoing, but when he learned he was under suspicion for murder and extortion, he quickly confessed to the crimes against Soviet property. He vehemently denied having anything to do with the murders. With a little bit more digging, police were able to verify that Dmitri was telling them the truth. He was a criminal, but he was not the killer they were looking for. The son had just set as university student Olga Lebedeva stood alone in Kishinev Central
追捕时间很短，德米特里被铁轨绊倒，迅速被捕。德米特里否认有任何不当行为，但当他得知自己因谋杀和勒索受到怀疑时，他很快承认了针对苏联财产的犯罪。他极力否认与谋杀案有任何关系。经过进一步挖掘，警方能够证实德米特里说的是实话。他是个罪犯，但他不是他们要找的凶手。太阳刚刚落山，大学生奥尔加·列别杰娃（Olga Lebedeva）独自站在基希讷乌中央

31
00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:55.000
Park waiting for her date. Several months prior, Olga had responded to a personal ad in the local newspaper and had been corresponding with the man ever since. This was the first time they were going to meet in person. Olga's date soon approached, carrying a bouquet of flowers. He handed them to her and immediately apologized, saying he couldn't stay for their date as some important business had just come up. He then turned around and hurried away.
公园等待约会对象。几个月前，奥尔加在当地报纸上回复了一则征友广告，此后一直与那名男子通信。这是他们第一次见面。奥尔加的约会对象很快走近，手里拿着一束花。他把花递给她，并立即道歉，说他因为刚处理了一些重要事务，无法留下来赴约。随后他转身匆匆离开。

32
00:21:55.000 --> 00:22:39.000
Confused, Olga decided to head home. As she walked through the park along a tree-lined path, she heard someone approaching from behind. Olga quickened her pace, so did the person behind her. Suddenly, Olga was jerked backwards and thrown to the ground. A man stood over her before pulling her into some bushes nearby. He wrapped a hand around Olga's neck and squeezed, using his other hand to hold up a knife. As Olga fought for her life, the contents of her bags spilled onto the ground.
困惑的奥尔加决定回家。当她走在公园里一条林荫小道上时，听到身后有人走近。奥尔加加快了脚步，身后的人也加快了脚步。突然，奥尔加被猛地向后一拽，摔倒在地。一个男人站在她上方，随后将她拖入附近的灌木丛。他用一只手掐住奥尔加的脖子，另一只手拿着一把刀。当奥尔加拼命挣扎时，包里的东西散落在地上。

33
00:22:39.000 --> 00:23:17.000
She grabbed the nearest item, her hairbrush, and jammed it as hard as she could into the man's groin. He released his grip, dropped his knife, and gripped his crotch as he curled over in pain. Olga scrambled to her feet. As she rushed back onto the footpath, her attacker yelled out, I will catch up with you, creature, and I will cut you into pieces. Olga ran as fast as she could, right into the path of someone who had slipped away from a birthday party early to head home.
她抓起最近的东西——她的发梳，尽全力猛地扎进男人的腹股沟。他松开了手，丢下刀，捂着裆部痛苦地蜷缩起来。奥尔加挣扎着站起身。当她冲回人行道时，袭击者大喊：我会抓住你的，畜生，我会把你剁成碎片。奥尔加拼命奔跑，正好撞上了一个为了早点回家而提前离开生日派对的人。

34
00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:59.000
They took her to the police station, where the officer on duty was intrigued to learn that Olga's attacker had threatened to cut her into pieces. Police across the city had been briefed about the unidentified killer who had been sending mutilated remains to Theodosius Glukarev. The officer was aware that in one of the notes the perpetrator had used the phrase, We will chop your daughter to pieces. Seeing Olga had survived an encounter with the killer, hundreds of police officers descended on Kishinev's Central Park to scour the area for clues.
他们把她带到了警察局，值班警官得知奥尔加的袭击者曾威胁要将她“剁成碎片”时感到很震惊。全市的警察都已接到关于那个向西奥多西·格卢卡列夫寄送残肢的身份不明凶手的简报。警官意识到，在其中一张字条中，作案者曾使用过“我们会把你女儿剁成碎片”这句话。看到奥尔加在与凶手的遭遇中幸存下来，数百名警察涌入基希讷乌中央公园，搜寻线索。

35
00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:48.000
They soon came upon a plot of freshly disturbed earth. The area was dug up, revealing a shallow grave containing the body of a young woman. Her shirt was torn open, and her trousers and underwear were pulled below her knees. There were multiple stub wounds to her chest and around her genitals. Most significantly, her head was missing. Police had just uncovered the body of Irina Trasin. Now they were absolutely certain that the same man who attacked Olga Lebedeva had killed Irina and that he had used the expansive parklands as his hunting ground.
他们很快发现了一块刚被翻动过的土地。该区域被挖开，露出了一个浅坑，里面埋着一名年轻女性的尸体。她的衬衫被撕开，裤子和内衣被拉到膝盖以下。她的胸部和生殖器周围有多处刺伤。最重要的是，她的头不见了。警方刚刚发现了伊琳娜·特拉森的尸体。现在他们完全确定，袭击奥尔加·列别杰娃的那个男人就是杀害伊琳娜的凶手，并且他一直将广阔的公园作为他的狩猎场。

36
00:24:48.000 --> 00:25:31.000
Olga struggled to recall much about her ordeal as it was dark and happened quickly, but something about her assailant seemed familiar. She was certain it was the same man she had met for a date 30 minutes earlier. Olga explained that she had been corresponding with this man for some time. The investigators asked if she had kept any of the letters. Lucky for them, she had kept them all. Each of the letters were handwritten and had been signed off with the sender's name, Alexander Skrinik.
奥尔加努力回忆关于她遭遇的细节，因为当时天很黑且发生得很快，但袭击者的某些特征让她感到熟悉。她确信这就是她30分钟前见面的那个男人。奥尔加解释说她已经与这个男人通信有一段时间了。调查人员问她是否保留了任何信件。幸运的是，她把信都留下了。每一封信都是手写的，并署有寄件人的名字：亚历山大·斯克里尼克（Alexander Skrinik）。

37
00:25:31.000 --> 00:26:11.000
The police were stunned. They knew Skrinik. Across most Eastern European countries, the name Alexander is commonly shortened to Sasha. Alexander Skrinik was Uncle Sasha, the man who had approached Theodosius' daughter with candy weeks earlier. A background check of Skrinik had ruled him out as a suspect, but now investigators were certain he was the killer they'd been looking for. They just needed to find some compelling evidence to prove it.
警方惊呆了。他们认识斯克里尼克。在大多数东欧国家，亚历山大这个名字通常缩写为萨沙。亚历山大·斯克里尼克就是萨沙叔叔，那个几周前带着糖果接近西奥多西女儿的男人。对斯克里尼克的背景调查曾将他排除在嫌疑人之外，但现在调查人员确信他就是他们一直在寻找的凶手。他们只需要找到一些令人信服的证据来证明这一点。

38
00:26:11.000 --> 00:26:53.000
No viable forensics had been found on Irina Trassen's head or body, nor on the unidentified severed hand left at Theodosius' door. This just left the extortion notes and the letters to Olga. A handwriting expert was brought in, but when he looked at the samples, he shrugged. The extortion notes had been printed in block capitals, whereas the letters were in Skrinik's cursive handwriting. It wasn't possible to conclusively compare the two. Meanwhile, Alexander Skrinik was called to attend the Military Registration and Enlistment
在伊琳娜·特拉森的头颅或尸体上，以及留在西奥多西门前的身份不明的断手上，都没有发现可用的法医证据。这只剩下勒索信和给奥尔加的信。一位笔迹专家被请来，但他看着样本耸了耸肩。勒索信是用大写印刷体打印的，而信件则是斯克里尼克的草书手写体。无法确凿地比较两者。与此同时，亚历山大·斯克里尼克被传唤到军事登记和征兵

39
00:26:53.000 --> 00:27:36.000
Office. At 27 years of age, Skrinik was still subject to Soviet conscription until his next birthday. He arrived promptly at the military office and was shown into an adjacent room. He, along with about 20 other conscripts, filled in the necessary paperwork. Afterwards, they were told that a military representative would be in touch soon. Alexander Skrinik then left the building. Unbeknownst to Skrinik, the entire registration process was a setup by police as a way to obtain his handwriting.
办公室。27岁的斯克里尼克在下次生日之前仍需服苏联兵役。他准时到达军事办公室，被带进了一个隔壁房间。他和其他约20名应征入伍者一起填写了必要的文件。之后，他们被告知军事代表很快会与他们联系。亚历山大·斯克里尼克随后离开了大楼。斯克里尼克不知道的是，整个登记过程是警方为了获取他的笔迹而设的局。

40
00:27:36.000 --> 00:28:29.000
The call, the staff, and the other conscripts had all been staged. The military registration papers were required to be completed in block capital letters. As soon as Skrinik left, the registration papers were given to the handwriting expert who was waiting behind the scenes. Within half an hour, the expert unequivocally concluded that the block letters in Skrinik's registration form were an exact match to those in the two extortion notes sent to Theodosius. Case file will be back shortly. Thank you for supporting us by listening to this episode's sponsors.
电话、工作人员和其他应征者都是安排好的。军事登记表要求用大写印刷体填写。斯克里尼克一离开，登记表就被交给了在幕后等待的笔迹专家。半小时内，专家明确断定斯克里尼克登记表上的大写字母与寄给西奥多西的两封勒索信中的字迹完全吻合。Case file稍后回来。感谢您通过收听本集赞助商的广告来支持我们。

