Thank you for listening to this episode's ads. By supporting our sponsors, you support case file to continue to deliver quality content. That evening, police arrived at Alexander Skrinik's apartment, only to be told by Skrinik's wife that her husband had just left to see a movie. A contingent of plainclothes police officers quickly descended on the Patriar Cinema in central Kishinyev. The film that was about to be shown was a Soviet disaster film called Aircrew, which depicted the story of a plane full of passengers trying to take off during an earthquake.
感谢您收听本集的广告。通过支持我们的赞助商，您支持Case file继续提供优质内容。那天晚上，警察赶到亚历山大·斯克里尼克的公寓，却被斯克里尼克的妻子告知，她丈夫刚出门去看电影。一队便衣警察迅速包围了基希讷乌市中心的帕特里亚电影院。即将放映的电影是一部名为《机组人员》（Aircrew）的苏联灾难片，讲述了一架载满乘客的飞机在地震中试图起飞的故事。

42
00:29:15.000 --> 00:29:54.000
Aircrew had debuted earlier in 1980, but due to its popularity, it was being re-screened to a sold-out audience. Police searched for Skrinik amongst the throng of cinema-goers milling outside the building and inside the foyer waiting for the movie to start. Eventually, they spotted Skrinik. He was approaching the cinema accompanied by a young woman. One quick-thinking detective approached the couple. He explained that the film was sold out, but he had two tickets he was willing to sell.
《机组人员》于1980年初首映，但由于广受欢迎，正在向满座的观众重映。警察在电影院外徘徊的影迷中以及等待电影开始的大厅里搜寻斯克里尼克。最终，他们发现了斯克里尼克。他正陪着一名年轻女子走向电影院。一名机智的侦探走近这对男女。他解释说电影票已售罄，但他有两张票愿意出售。

43
00:29:54.000 --> 00:30:37.000
Skrinik was interested. The detective suggested that they walk around the side of the building where it was much quieter in order to make the exchange. Skrinik and the young woman happily accompanied the detective. Once they were away from the crowd, other officers converged on Skrinik and placed him under arrest. At the police station, Alexander Skrinik remained indignant. He denied having done anything wrong and pointed to his Government Labor Award and membership of the Soviet Communist Party as proof of his good character and innocence.
斯克里尼克很感兴趣。侦探建议他们走到大楼侧面，那里安静得多，以便进行交易。斯克里尼克和那名年轻女子高兴地陪同侦探前往。一旦他们远离人群，其他警察便围住斯克里尼克并将他逮捕。在警察局，亚历山大·斯克里尼克依然愤愤不平。他否认做了任何错事，并指着他的政府劳动奖章和苏联共产党党员身份，作为他品行端正和清白的证明。

44
00:30:37.000 --> 00:31:23.000
However, once investigators revealed the ruse at the enlistment office and the handwriting analysis evidence they had against him, Skrinik abandoned his charade. Skrinik then made a surprise confession. Arena Trassen was not his first murder victim. Several years earlier in the mid-1970s, he had been living and working in Yakutia, a sparsely populated Soviet region in the Far East of Russia. There, Skrinik met and murdered a flight attendant named Nina Puganova. After killing Nina, Skrinik removed her breasts and genitals before dumping her body.
然而，当调查人员揭露了征兵办公室的诡计以及他们掌握的笔迹分析证据后，斯克里尼克放弃了伪装。斯克里尼克随后做出了令人震惊的供述。伊琳娜·特拉森并不是他的第一个受害者。几年前的70年代中期，他曾在俄罗斯远东地区人口稀少的苏联地区雅库特生活和工作。在那里，斯克里尼克遇见并谋杀了一名名叫尼娜·普加诺娃（Nina Puganova）的空姐。杀害尼娜后，斯克里尼克切除了她的乳房和生殖器，然后抛弃了她的尸体。

45
00:31:23.000 --> 00:32:02.000
The remains were later discovered, however authorities at the time were unable to solve Nina's murder. Skrinik disclosed that he had stabbed Arena Trassen to death after meeting her for ice cream at the park where her body was later found. He decapitated Arena post-mortem, kept her head, before burying her body in a shallow grave. Skrinik's third and final victim was a woman named Anastasia Mikhailova. Like Arena before her, Skrinik had met Anastasia for ice cream before stabbing her to death
遗体后来被发现，但当时的当局无法破获尼娜的谋杀案。斯克里尼克透露，他在公园里与伊琳娜·特拉森见面吃冰淇淋后，将她刺死，尸体后来就是在那里被发现的。他在死后将伊琳娜斩首，保留了她的头颅，然后将她的尸体埋在一个浅坑里。斯克里尼克的第三个也是最后一个受害者是一个名叫阿纳斯塔西娅·米哈伊洛娃（Anastasia Mikhailova）的女人。像之前的伊琳娜一样，斯克里尼克在与阿纳斯塔西娅见面吃冰淇淋后将她刺死，

46
00:32:02.000 --> 00:32:41.000
and mutilating her body. This time Skrinik had kept Anastasia's severed hand as a souvenir. Having already discovered Arena's headless body, police probed Skrinik for the whereabouts of Anastasia's remains. Skrinik said that Anastasia was buried in a different park and offered to take them to the exact location. The following day, he escorted investigators to an area of Woodland. He pointed to the exact location where officers should start digging.
并残害了她的尸体。这一次，斯克里尼克保留了阿纳斯塔西娅被切断的手作为纪念品。在已经发现了伊琳娜的无头尸体后，警方追问斯克里尼克关于阿纳斯塔西娅遗体的下落。斯克里尼克说阿纳斯塔西娅被埋在另一个公园，并主动提出带他们去确切地点。第二天，他陪同调查人员来到一片林地。他指出了警察应该开始挖掘的确切位置。

47
